}^{x},$ we take the graph of $y={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}$ and stretch it vertically by a scale factor of  $k.$ Under the action of this transformation, the $y$-intercept is mapped from $(0,1)$ to $(0,k).$\n\nComparing the point $(0,1.5)$ on the graph to $(0,k),$ we see that we must have $k=1.5.$"}]}
